# GitHub owns these — issue forms and workflow templates, not knowledge
.github/

# The frontmatter contract corpus — parser inputs, deliberately including malformed ones.
# Test data is not knowledge, and half of it would fail `check` on purpose.
tests/fixtures/

# Eval scenario briefs and rubrics — inputs to `tessl eval run`, addressed to a grading agent,
# not to a reader of this repository's documentation. Same reasoning as tests/fixtures/ above.
evals/

# A vendored tool's own files and its memory, not this repository's knowledge. The walk
# cannot descend into a dot-directory, so `index` can never list these; naming them here is
# the remedy `coverage` itself advises.
.tessl/
